---
title: Tuna Fish Enchiladas
servings: 4
time: 25 min
tags: tuna, enchiladas, quick, dinner, seafood
cuisine: Tex-Mex
course: main
source: tuna_fish_enchiladas.png
---

Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).

Coat a #flat baking pan{} with @butter spray{}. Lay @flour tortillas{4} flat on the pan.

Spoon @red enchilada sauce{1/2%cup} evenly over one half of each tortilla.

Thinly layer flaked @canned tuna{2%cans}(drained) and @chopped green chilies{1%can}(4 oz) over the sauce.

Top with shredded @cheddar cheese{1%cup} and diced @tomatoes{1%cup}.

Fold the uncovered half of each tortilla over the filling to form half-moon enchiladas.

Spoon remaining @red enchilada sauce{1/2%cup} over top and sprinkle with remaining @cheddar cheese{1/2%cup}.

Bake at 375°F until the cheese is melted and bubbling, about ~{10%minutes}.
